    "body": "## Independent exact-head review - Chat03B2 capability generation SQL foundation\n\n**Reviewed exact HEAD** `c0e6ccb11d8302b1e6f7095a063d5c93f5313f98`, tree `3bfe3ddb88bbeebeee096572eaf6f634e1192c68`. Existing Draft PR #443 remains OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED, clean/mergeable, base Draft PR #442 `f1a4592e5b72c5d54d0f72c558dbc37c08b07733`; parent Draft PR #441 `6ad90e6e86d528b1858776477fb7e8680f89115d`. Comparison to base: **ahead 2, behind 0** (the final SHA's first parent is `818ef5bc507521fdbebf888f7c76d68cf6a60227`, not the PR442 HEAD directly); exactly two added files and no other changed paths: `gameplay-server/migrations/0004_capability_generation.sql`, `gameplay-server/test/test_chat03b2_capability_generation_sql.py`.\n\n**Verdict: `PASS_NARROW_CAPABILITY_GENERATION_SCHEMA` / `NOT_REVOCATION_AUTHORIZATION_OR_DEPLOYMENT_PASS`.** Migration 0004 is additive: persisted `status` restricted to `active/revoked`, `generation` positive SQLite integer limited to JS safe integer max, default 1 for schema initialization only, trigger guards numerical regression. Legacy digest, participant/battle/side data, uniqueness, FK and lookup index preserved in actual SQLite migration tests. The new seven unittest cases cover numeric REAL affinity, invalid values, monotonicity, transactional rollback, keys/FK and index use. Historical generation=1 MUST NOT be treated as issuance provenance or permission to release encrypted recovery.\n\n**Exact-head CI independently verified via GitHub run metadata, jobs and actual logs:** [CAS SQL PR run 39963168114](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963168114) SUCCESS (46/46 Python discovery, all 7 new suite cases visible; Wrangler local legacy path and retired runner 5/5 PASS); [CAS SQL push run 39963159709](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963159709) SUCCESS; [Private Gameplay API push 39963159700](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963159700) and [PR run 39963167820](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963167820) SUCCESS (original 22/22 hosted-harness offline safety, original local workerd integration); [Forensics push 39963159711](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963159711) and [PR run 39963167800](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963167800) SUCCESS. All run head SHA `c0e6ccb...`. **Local Wrangler Worker path does not apply migration 0004; do not count it as D1-v4 acceptance.** Codex local policy validation and git diff check are reported but not executed by this reviewer.\n\n**Security caveats and next prerequisite:** At this narrow storage-only phase SQL permits `UPDATE status='active'` on a previously revoked row without raising generation, plus reset via row replacement if entrusted to a writer; the model cannot yet guarantee irreversible revocation or atomic authorized commit. This is **outside the scope of the additive foundation** but MUST be explicitly forbidden/controlled in the future trusted capability lifecycle + SQL CAS authorization gate. The existing Worker still looks up digests without checking `status`/`generation` atomically during gameplay transition; current recovery 0003 can return original ciphertext on admin replay. Future implementation must enforce status/generation and credential rotation/revoke in the SAME atomic protected mutation and close stale recovery, preserve restricted Worker-only scheduler transitions, and test D1-specific binding/transaction semantics. Historic creation rows remain fail-closed when recovery lifecycle is migrated.\n\n**Disposition:** two-file schema foundation and independent CI PASS, no follow-on permission to deploy 0004 in isolation, perform Cloudflare/hosted D1 operations, merge any Draft PR or main, onboard real users, approve retention/backup/keyring policy, or claim Safari/runtime acceptance. Checkpoint + Recovery user governance remains mandatory. Further work must be a separately scoped synthetic/local-only atom with fresh exact SHA and independent review.",
