    "body": "## Scope\n\nAdd the minimum additive D1/SQLite schema foundation for persisted capability status and generation, stacked directly on Draft PR #442 at `f1a4592e5b72c5d54d0f72c558dbc37c08b07733`.\n\nOnly:\n- `gameplay-server/migrations/0004_capability_generation.sql`\n- `gameplay-server/test/test_chat03b2_capability_generation_sql.py`\n\nThe migration preserves capability rows and existing keys, adds `status` constrained to `active` / `revoked`, and adds positive safe-integer `generation`. Historical rows receive generation 1 as schema initialization only. It does NOT prove original credential issuance.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFinal head: `c0e6ccb11d8302b1e6f7095a063d5c93f5313f98`.\n\n- New suite: 7/7 PASS.\n- Full Python discovery: 46/46 PASS, including the new file via the existing `test_*.py` CI pattern.\n- Repository policy validation and `git diff --check`: PASS.\n- Exact-head SQL/CAS: [push run #39963159709](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963159709) and [PR run #39963168114](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963168114) SUCCESS.\n- Exact-head local Worker/D1 and offline safety workflow: [push run #39963159700](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963159700) SUCCESS.\n- Exact-head AI Forensics: [push run #39963159711](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/39963159711) SUCCESS.\n\nTests run actual migrations 0001-0003 before seeding synthetic battles, capabilities, recovery, receipts and outbox rows; then verify migration preservation, old-row metadata, integral numeric bindings, range/status checks, monotonicity, atomic rollback, uniqueness, FK behavior and lookup-index use.\n\n## Deployment block\n\nThis migration is not authorized for deployment. Persisting `revoked` does not make the Worker reject a token. Before deployment, a coordinated Worker/SQL authorization fence must check capability digest, status and generation in the same atomic transaction as each protected battle mutation. Creation-recovery issuance, generation binding, rotation/revocation closure and their lifecycle must also be implemented and reviewed. Historical 0003 encrypted recovery rows remain untrusted for future lifecycle migration; generation 1 is not issuance evidence.\n\nNo HTTP endpoints, credential issuance, creation-recovery changes, hosted D1, deployment, or parent PR edits are included.",
